---
import Operations from "../../layouts/Operations.astro";
import DashboardDrawing from "../../components/DashboardDrawing.astro";
import WorkspaceControls from "../../components/WorkspaceControls.astro";
---
<Operations title="Publishers & safety" description="Verify publisher ownership, manage blocked material, and keep a record of each decision." section="security">
  <p id="security-status" tabindex="-1" class="operations-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking reviewer access…</p>
  <button class="button secondary" id="security-refresh" type="button">Refresh security status</button>
  <a id="security-signin" href="/auth/github/start?returnTo=%2Fadmin%2Fsecurity" hidden>Sign in with GitHub</a>
  <div id="security-content" hidden data-workspace-panels class="security-control-room">
    <WorkspaceControls label="Registry security tasks" entries={[["security-ownership-panel", "Verify publishers", "Check identity and ownership"], ["security-material-panel", "Block material", "Record digest restrictions"], ["security-blocks-panel", "Current blocks", "Inspect active restrictions"]]} />
    <section id="security-ownership-panel" data-workspace-panel class="operations-panel" aria-labelledby="verification-heading"><div class="task-panel-heading"><p class="step-label">01 / Know the publisher</p><h2 id="verification-heading">Verify a publisher</h2><DashboardDrawing section="security-ownership-panel" compact /></div><p>Verify someone you have independently identified: enter their publisher namespace, link to the GitHub profile or website you checked, and record how you confirmed ownership. The badge appears on their listings. You can remove it with a new decision. Verification does not approve their packages or bypass review.</p>
      <form id="security-verification" class="task-form"><fieldset><legend>Record a namespace decision</legend>
        <div class="form-field"><label for="security-namespace">Publisher namespace</label><input id="security-namespace" name="namespace" required pattern="[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,62}" maxlength="63" /></div>
        <label for="security-verified"><input id="security-verified" name="verified" type="checkbox" /> Mark ownership verified (unchecked removes verification)</label>
        <div class="form-field"><label for="security-proof">HTTPS ownership proof URL (required when marking verified)</label><input id="security-proof" name="proof" placeholder="https://github.com/publisher-account" type="url" maxlength="2000" /></div>
        <div class="form-field"><label for="security-verification-reason">Decision reason; describe the evidence reviewed</label><textarea id="security-verification-reason" name="reason" required maxlength="2000"></textarea></div>
        <label><input type="checkbox" required /> I have checked the namespace and intended verification state.</label><button class="button" type="submit">Record verification decision</button>
      </fieldset><p role="status" data-result></p></form>
    </section>
    <section id="security-material-panel" data-workspace-panel class="operations-panel" aria-labelledby="block-heading"><div class="task-panel-heading"><p class="step-label">02 / Respond to package material</p><h2 id="block-heading">Block harmful material</h2><DashboardDrawing section="security-material-panel" compact /></div><p>A digest may identify an archive or a packaged file. Blocking revokes approved releases that contain it. Publish updated signed metadata promptly; recording a block alone does not deliver authenticated revocation to installed clients.</p>
      <form id="security-block" class="task-form"><fieldset><legend>Block one digest</legend><div class="form-field"><label for="security-digest">Exact lowercase SHA-256 digest</label><input id="security-digest" name="digest" required pattern="[a-f0-9]{64}" maxlength="64" autocomplete="off" /></div><div class="form-field"><label for="security-block-reason">Block reason</label><textarea id="security-block-reason" name="reason" required maxlength="2000"></textarea></div><label><input type="checkbox" required /> I understand this can revoke approved releases containing this material.</label><button class="button" type="submit">Block digest and affected approved releases</button></fieldset><p role="status" data-result></p></form>
      <details><summary>Import a bounded digest batch</summary><form id="security-batch" class="task-form"><fieldset><legend>Block 1–100 unique digests</legend><p>One line per digest: lowercase SHA-256, a space, then the reason. The request is limited to 64 KiB and applied atomically.</p><div class="form-field"><label for="security-batch-value">Digest and reason lines</label><textarea id="security-batch-value" name="entries" required maxlength="65536" rows="8"></textarea></div><label><input type="checkbox" required /> I reviewed every digest and understand affected approved releases may be revoked.</label><button class="button" type="submit">Block all listed digests</button></fieldset><p role="status" data-result></p></form></details>
    </section>
    <section id="security-blocks-panel" data-workspace-panel class="operations-ledger" aria-labelledby="blocked-heading"><div class="task-panel-heading"><p class="step-label">03 / Active restrictions</p><h2 id="blocked-heading">Currently blocked</h2><DashboardDrawing section="security-blocks-panel" compact /></div><p>Up to 500 newest blocks are shown, not a complete lifetime history. Removing a block does not restore revoked releases; review and signed publication remain separate.</p><ul id="security-blocked"></ul></section>
  </div>
</Operations>
<script>import "../../scripts/review-security";</script>
